{"name":"Coconut Twist","hex":"#f7f1e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coconut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit of the coconut palm (not a true nut), Cocos nucifera, having a fibrous husk surrounding a large seed.","A hard-shelled seed of this fruit, having white flesh and a fluid-filled central cavity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut"},{"term":"twist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A twisting force.","Anything twisted, or the act of twisting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn the ends of something, usually thread, rope etc., in opposite directions, often using force.","To join together by twining one part around another."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twist (confectionery)","blocks":[{"text":"Twist is a bite-sized confectionery produced by Freia, primarily for the Scandinavian market. Twist is sold in bags, and each bag contains a variety of pieces, mostly consisting of chocolates with some sort of filling in the center. New pieces are added and old ones discontinued frequently. Only two pieces, Lakris (licorice) and Cocos, have existed since the product was launched. The name Twist refers to the way each piece is wrapped."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Twist-sk%C3%A5l_%282017%29.jpg/330px-Twist-sk%C3%A5l_%282017%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twist_(confectionery)"},{"title":"Twist (cocktail garnish)","blocks":[{"text":"A twist is a piece of citrus zest used as a cocktail garnish, generally for decoration and to add flavor when added to a mixed drink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/The_perfect_martini.jpg/330px-The_perfect_martini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twist_(cocktail_garnish)"